WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.420
A delegation of Houthi rebels has arrived
in Sweden for talks with the Yemeni government

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:02.420
aimed at ending a four-year war that has led
to the worst humanitarian catastrophe in recent

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.420
times.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.420
But distrust between the warring parties is
high.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:05.420
Passports and tickets in hand, for a journey
many hope will bring peace.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.940
A delegation of Houthi rebels waiting to board
their flight to Sweden.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.800
The UN's special envoy Martin Griffiths has
been instrumental in setting up the talks

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.580
with the Yemeni government.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:22.530
Such is the distrust between the two sides,
the rebels wouldn't get on the plane without

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:27.640
him.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:33.220
Our basic guarantee is the presence of the
UN envoy with us on the same flight.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.899
This is the only guarantee we have for going
there."

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:43.909
The evacuation of 50 wounded Houthi fighters
from the warzone on has also helped built

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:48.980
confidence in the talks -- with the conflict
locked in stalemate.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:54.370
The Houthis -- backed by Iran -- control the
northwest of the country, including the capital

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.639
Sanaa, which they took in 2015.

00:00:56.639 --> 00:01:02.109
The government -- backed by Saudi Arabia and
the UAE -- has set up base in Aden, in the

00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:07.030
south.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:11.640
Four years of conflict have left thousands
dead and created what's been described as

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.760
the worst humanitarian crisis in recent history.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:21.780
With Yemen's economy crippled, more than 14
million people -- many of them children -- are

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.670
facing starvation.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:31.159
It is a country at war, as I've heard many
say, this is a country on the brink of catastrophe.

00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:38.450
This is not a country on the break of catastrophe,
this is a country that is in a catastrophe.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:43.999
A catastrophe that's unfolded in full view
of the whole world, but one many say has been

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:45.439
ignored.

00:01:45.439 --> 00:02:17.569
The hope is the talks will result in a truce,
allowing food and aid to reach those who need

00:02:17.569 --> 00:05:22.139
it most.

